## Solution 2: Sort (O(NlogN) time)

In this question, we were asked to return k largest numbers in the array. The question asked us to return the result in sorted order. I'm using `sort()` to sort the array in non-descending order, and return the last k elements. For example, if the `arr = [-3, -4, 5], k = 3`, the array will become `[-4, -3, 5]`. It will return the elements from index `len(arr) - k = 3 - 3 = 0` to the end of the array. It will return `[-4, -3, 5]`.

```python
# Solution 2: Sort (O(NlogN) time)
class Solution:
    def maximum(self, arr, k):
        arr.sort()
        return arr[len(arr) - k:]
